<details><summary>Extended reading appendix</summary><p>The linked bibliography includes foundations, effectiveness, implementation, technology support and the Kingston–Nash correction. Scope notes distinguish source types and limits; earlier digital-assessment studies do not establish Codex or WorkBuddy effectiveness.</p><div class="actions"><a class="download" href={`${resources}reading-list.html`} download>Download reading appendix</a><a href={`${resources}reading-list.html`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the annotated bibliography</a></div></details>
<details><summary>Evidence drawer: what can we reasonably expect?</summary><p>Formative assessment can support learning, but effects depend on implementation and how evidence is used. More quizzes, more feedback or AI alone do not guarantee improvement. This workshop makes no promise to double learning.</p><p>Keep process and outcome separate: a sound process still requires evidence of actual development. No observed gain does not automatically make the process invalid. Unsound interpretation or use does not warrant the intended formative benefit, although unrelated learning may still occur.</p></details>

<details><summary>Optional research contrast: receiving feedback or acting on it?</summary><p>A supplied speaking-course slide sequence, attributed to “Li &amp; Gu (2026); 李加义 (2026)”, compares conversation only, conversation plus feedback, and conversation plus feedback and action. All three groups keep journals; only the third condition requires an exercise and implementing a strategy.</p><p>What action is intended to close a learning gap, and what fresh speaking evidence would show whether it helped? Reflection or receiving comments alone does not demonstrate development.</p><p class="source-note">Supplied presentation evidence; publication identity for this three-group version is unverified. It is distinct from Li &amp; Gu (2024). No superiority or causal claim is made here.</p></details>

<details><summary>Tool preparation and classroom boundaries</summary><p><a href="https://www.workbuddy.cn/">WorkBuddy download</a> · <a href="https://cloud.tencent.com/document/product/1831/134387">Install guide</a> · <a href="https://cloud.tencent.com/document/product/1831/134389">Getting started</a> · <a href="https://cloud.tencent.com/document/product/1831/134400">Preview guide</a></p><p>Install, sign in and try a tiny HTML before arrival. WorkBuddy documents Windows 10+ x64 and macOS 12+. Generation needs internet and may be subject to usage limits. Use paired work or the prepared HTML/paper fallback; no compulsory paid subscription. Follow normal permission checks and use fictional data.</p><p>Codex and WorkBuddy are demonstration/build tools. This workshop does not imply sponsorship by OpenAI or Tencent. The completed lab uses fixed teacher-approved hints locally, with no runtime AI or class response collection.</p></details>
<p class="source-note">The design continues April Jiawei Zhang’s January 2026 ILTA formative-assessment workshop foundations: goals and criteria, feedback, peer/self-assessment and learner agency. All learner samples and cases here are fictional. Workshop examples are educational designs, not validated assessment instruments.</p>
